Yeah.

1576
01:12:01.060 --> 01:12:03.080
He was really upset.

1577
01:12:03.080 --> 01:12:03.500
He was hurt.

1578
01:12:03.500 --> 01:12:05.880
He was hurting, and he just sort of lashed out.

1579
01:12:06.080 --> 01:12:07.660
I didn't think it needed to be long.

1580
01:12:07.780 --> 01:12:08.560
I thought it was perfect.

1581
01:12:08.720 --> 01:12:13.740
But I also love, and this is something we've talked about a lot, Greg, is that these characters

1582
01:12:13.740 --> 01:12:14.780
are flawed people.

1583
01:12:15.020 --> 01:12:16.140
They're not perfect people.

1584
01:12:16.380 --> 01:12:19.440
So they're going to have moments like Pam was petty.

1585
01:12:19.640 --> 01:12:21.200
I think Pam has been petty.

1586
01:12:22.520 --> 01:12:28.480
And my character is certainly, we've talked about, my character is certainly not the nicest

1587
01:12:28.480 --> 01:12:30.140
person, and-

1588
01:12:30.140 --> 01:12:33.400
You went the longest, being not the nicest of any character.

1589
01:12:33.640 --> 01:12:33.980
Yes.

1590
01:12:34.180 --> 01:12:38.240
And which was great, because then when we got into season nine, and I was kind of casting

1591
01:12:38.240 --> 01:12:42.420
