JT wrote in to ask who was the actual person who jumped in the water.

1612
01:13:38.340 --> 01:13:41.580
And a lot of people are asking, what happened to that person?

1613
01:13:42.680 --> 01:13:43.120
Yes.

1614
01:13:43.220 --> 01:13:46.940
Well, that was one of the non-Dunder Mifflin people on the boat.

1615
01:13:47.220 --> 01:13:51.520
And as I recall, he was not supposed to jump off the boat.

1616
01:13:52.220 --> 01:13:59.360
As I recall, I mean, I may be blowing this because it was a while ago, but I think there

1617
01:13:59.360 --> 01:14:03.540
was a little bit of shock that one of the extras jumped off the boat in that take.

1618
01:14:03.640 --> 01:14:07.860
And I think we were probably not supposed to let him jump off the boat.

1619
01:14:08.940 --> 01:14:15.680
Well, on the DVD commentary, Greg, you said he really jumped out of the window into the

1620
01:14:15.680 --> 01:14:16.840
freezing cold water.

1621
01:14:17.020 --> 01:14:17.240
Yeah.

1622
01:14:17.660 --> 01:14:25.900
And you said that you always felt bad that there is no, like, this person jumped into the

1623
01:14:25.900 --> 01:14:26.600
It wasn't on camera.

1624
01:14:26.700 --> 01:14:27.860
It wasn't on camera.

1625
01:14:28.240 --> 01:14:29.920
He didn't jump in a boat.

1626
01:14:30.160 --> 01:14:31.340
He didn't jump in a boat.

1627
01:14:31.340 --> 01:14:33.260
Like, he had to be fished out of the water.

1628
01:14:33.480 --> 01:14:34.640
It could have been just a rubber dinghy there.

1629
01:14:35.020 --> 01:14:37.180
I believe it only happened the one time.

1630
01:14:37.360 --> 01:14:38.060
Yeah, I think so.

1631
01:14:38.180 --> 01:14:44.020
I think he went, I think he may have either misinterpreted some direction or he just was

