01:14:44.020 --> 01:14:44.820
super enthusiastic.

1633
01:14:44.820 --> 01:14:49.980
I don't, I have a slight memory of that being a little too gorilla.

1634
01:14:51.420 --> 01:14:54.300
That's like Kent was out there running that shot.

1635
01:14:55.480 --> 01:14:59.260
Kent was in the boat that was supposed to catch him, but he went and took the shot.

1636
01:14:59.940 --> 01:15:05.700
Well, I loved at, so this is around 17 minutes, 34 seconds for my time code people, but I love

1637
01:15:05.700 --> 01:15:09.980
that the Dunder Mifflin employees know immediately that there's no emergency.

1638
01:15:10.320 --> 01:15:14.060
And like, even like Kevin and Angela, like we're in a booth together.

1639
01:15:14.360 --> 01:15:16.280
Oscar, I guess, is off somewhere being snarky.

1640
01:15:16.640 --> 01:15:19.060
And we're like, no, no, guys, no, no, there's nothing.

1641
01:15:19.200 --> 01:15:20.280
Right, you're trying to calm it down.

1642
01:15:20.380 --> 01:15:20.880
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1643
01:15:20.980 --> 01:15:24.300
And you pan across all the different Dunder Mifflin employees and they're like, oh God,

1644
01:15:24.420 --> 01:15:24.960
here we go.

1645
01:15:24.960 --> 01:15:27.280
So, but the rest of the boat doesn't know.

1646
01:15:29.040 --> 01:15:30.220
Well, this, oh, go ahead.

1647
01:15:30.400 --> 01:15:30.900
What were you going to say?

1648
01:15:31.500 --> 01:15:35.100
Well, I was just saying this was leading up to him being handcuffed on the roof.

1649
01:15:35.320 --> 01:15:35.680
Yes.

1650
01:15:35.800 --> 01:15:36.080
Yes.

1651
01:15:36.080 --> 01:15:45.880
And the kind of secret impetus for this whole episode was that, you know, we had come on

1652
01:15:45.880 --> 01:15:52.900
the air in the first season and we were given, you know, six episodes and we didn't do a great

1653
01:15:52.900 --> 01:15:53.860
job in the ratings.

1654
01:15:54.920 --> 01:15:59.220
And there was a lot of question whether we'd get invited back.

1655
01:15:59.540 --> 01:16:08.020
And so, at one point in between the seasons, Kevin Riley said, come in and, you know, pitch

1656
01:16:08.020 --> 01:16:09.220
me a new take on the show.

1657
01:16:09.360 --> 01:16:11.760
Like, why should I bring you guys back?

1658
01:16:12.240 --> 01:16:14.300
Oh my gosh, pressure.

1659
01:16:14.660 --> 01:16:15.580
There was a lot of pressure.

1660
01:16:15.580 --> 01:16:25.520
And so, I had initially kind of thought that The Office was such a special, unique show,

1661
01:16:25.640 --> 01:16:28.960
which I had so much respect for, that I wouldn't change very much on it.

1662
01:16:29.120 --> 01:16:32.120
And I realized that I needed to change something.

1663
01:16:32.320 --> 01:16:38.900
And I had some experience with this with King of the Hill in making Hank likable, the lead

1664
01:16:38.900 --> 01:16:39.580
of King of the Hill.

1665
01:16:39.580 --> 01:16:44.060
And he had certain qualities that were invented to keep him likable.

1666
01:16:44.200 --> 01:16:47.360
And so, I was like, oh, this isn't really that different.

1667
01:16:47.440 --> 01:16:53.500
You know, because Michael has some negative qualities and I just got to find a way to give

1668
01:16:53.500 --> 01:16:56.060
him some stories that are going to warm him up.

1669
01:16:56.180 --> 01:17:04.740
And so, I wrote out a bunch of story ideas somewhere, like in probably in Norm's.

1670
01:17:04.860 --> 01:17:06.140
No, we weren't at Norm's yet.

1671
01:17:06.140 --> 01:17:11.180
But that was my go-to place in the mornings on Sherman Way and Woodman.

1672
01:17:11.360 --> 01:17:16.180
But yeah, so I was in some, you know, coffee shop and I wrote down a bunch of moments that

1673
01:17:16.180 --> 01:17:17.300
I thought would warm him up.

1674
01:17:17.400 --> 01:17:24.840
And one of them was that, for instance, that the, you know, that even though the staff finds

1675
01:17:24.840 --> 01:17:27.700
him irritating, they'll back him against an outsider.

1676
01:17:27.920 --> 01:17:30.360
And so, that was like the end of Dundee's.

1677
01:17:31.680 --> 01:17:36.220
And, you know, one of them was like, he should be good at his job, which happened in the client.

1678
01:17:36.460 --> 01:17:38.300
He actually was a good salesperson.

1679
01:17:41.920 --> 01:17:48.320
And this one was that he should give a piece of really good advice to somebody that the

1680
01:17:48.320 --> 01:17:52.820
audience was going to be happy that that advice was transferred, you know.

1681
01:17:52.960 --> 01:17:55.440
And you'd be like, yeah, good for you, Michael.

1682
01:17:55.660 --> 01:18:01.980
And so, it was sort of all about him telling Jim to never give up on the top of that thing.

1683
01:18:02.420 --> 01:18:02.900
BFD.

1684
01:18:03.480 --> 01:18:04.620
Yeah, BFD, right?

1685
01:18:04.920 --> 01:18:05.920
Engaged ain't married.

1686
01:18:06.380 --> 01:18:06.600
Yeah.

1687
01:18:08.000 --> 01:18:10.060
But that's what the audience wanted to see.

1688
01:18:10.320 --> 01:18:11.960
You know, Jim was so sad.

1689
01:18:12.080 --> 01:18:15.480
You wanted somebody to give him some hope and keep this Jim Pam thing going.

1690
01:18:15.620 --> 01:18:17.640
And so, Michael kind of stepped in.

1691
01:18:17.760 --> 01:18:25.000
And I took the never, ever, ever give up from actually Winston Churchill's speech, which,

1692
01:18:25.500 --> 01:18:26.520
you know, was-

1693
01:18:26.520 --> 01:18:27.820
This is perfectly you.

1694
01:18:27.820 --> 01:18:28.560
This is so nerdy of me, right?

1695
01:18:28.560 --> 01:18:29.700
This is perfectly you.

1696
01:18:29.700 --> 01:18:34.340
Yeah, but like, I always choke up at the speeches of Winston Churchill in World War II

1697
01:18:34.340 --> 01:18:37.060
and, you know, fight him on the beaches, you know.

1698
01:18:37.140 --> 01:18:41.420
And he has something where he says, never, ever, ever, ever give in, you know.

1699
01:18:41.540 --> 01:18:43.400
And I was like, that's cool.

1700
01:18:43.400 --> 01:18:45.480
I'm going to crib that for Michael.

1701
01:18:46.540 --> 01:18:47.580
Well, it worked.

1702
01:18:47.580 --> 01:18:50.740
And it also worked for me, like, on a different level for Michael.

1703
01:18:50.860 --> 01:18:51.840
Like, it works for Jim.

1704
01:18:52.120 --> 01:18:56.480
But for Michael, the whole episode, he just wanted someone to feel inspired by him.

